# Financial Friday v0.5.0 Sprint – Advisor Intelligence

## Sprint Objective

Version **0.5.0** marks the transition from building a financial application to building an intelligent financial advisor.

The primary objective of this sprint is **not** to add new user-facing features. Instead, this sprint establishes the philosophical and behavioral foundation that will guide all future development.

Every design and engineering decision should support the mission of creating the world's most trusted AI financial advisor.

---

# Sprint Goals

## 1. Finalize Product Documentation

Complete the foundational documents that define Financial Friday.

### Deliverables

- Final Constitution
- Vision & Mission
- Advisor Intelligence Specification (AIS) v1.0

---

## 2. Audit the Existing Codebase

Perform a complete review of the current application to understand its current state before architectural design begins.

### Review Areas

- Project structure
- Folder organization
- Existing screens
- Firebase integration
- Authentication
- Routing
- State management
- Current dependencies
- Technical debt
- Opportunities for refactoring

### Deliverable

- Codebase Audit Report

---

## 3. Advisor Intelligence Design

Translate the Advisor's guiding philosophy into a comprehensive behavioral specification.

### Define

- Recommendation Engine
- Priority Engine
- Confidence Model
- Transparency System
- Memory Model
- Behavioral Analysis
- Goal Management
- Financial Story
- Emergency Mode
- Ethical Boundaries
- Advisor Operating Modes
- Continuous Improvement
- Decision Flow
- Knowledge & Evidence Sources

### Deliverable

- Advisor Intelligence Specification (AIS) v1.0

---

# Success Criteria

The sprint is considered complete when:

- The Constitution has been finalized.
- The Vision & Mission have been completed.
- The Advisor Intelligence Specification (AIS) v1.0 has been completed and approved.
- A complete audit of the existing codebase has been performed.
- The project is prepared for the Advisor Architecture Blueprint sprint.

---

# Guiding Principles

During this sprint we will prioritize:

- Simplicity
- Scalability
- Transparency
- Maintainability
- Security
- User Trust
- Long-term Thinking

Every engineering decision should support the principles established in the Financial Friday Constitution.

---

# Out of Scope

The following items are intentionally excluded from this sprint unless required to complete the Advisor Intelligence
